    "answer": {
      "short": "Carbon: $2.8\\text{ cm}$; gold: $5.4\\text{ cm}$; radium: $8.6\\text{ cm}$.",
      "worked": "The same enlargement factor applies to every radius. Since $25\\text{ pm}$ is represented by $1\\text{ cm}$, divide each actual radius in picometres by 25 to obtain its drawing radius in centimetres.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Carbon drawing radius}&=\\frac{70}{25}\\times1\\text{ cm}=2.8\\text{ cm}\\\\\\text{Gold drawing radius}&=\\frac{135}{25}\\times1\\text{ cm}=5.4\\text{ cm}\\\\\\text{Radium drawing radius}&=\\frac{215}{25}\\times1\\text{ cm}=8.6\\text{ cm}\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
